WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.117 --> 00:00:10.486
[in Mandarin] I have been helping my family farm 
since I was in school.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:19.824
Hsieh is one of hundreds of farmers in Taiwan
that grow atemoya

00:00:19.824 --> 00:00:21.397
a variety of custard apple.

00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:26.499
[in Mandarin] The texture is rather chewy.

00:00:26.499 --> 00:00:30.228
[in Mandarin] It is sweet, but it has a hint of sour, 
making the flavor unique.

00:00:31.624 --> 00:00:34.724
It’s one of the island’s most popular
fruit exports.

00:00:34.724 --> 00:00:39.187
Every season, farmers like Hsieh export around
14 million kilos.

00:00:39.187 --> 00:00:42.458
And 90% percent of that goes to China.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:49.000
But in September of 2021, China banned 
all imports of atemoya.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.989
They claimed they had pests.

00:00:52.062 --> 00:00:56.329
[in Mandarin] I was surprised it finally happened.

00:00:56.329 --> 00:01:00.149
Overnight, Hsieh lost 70 percent of his orders.

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:04.769
But this story is about more than just 
fruit, pests, or trade.

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:09.594
Atemoyas are a symbol of deep tensions 
between Taiwan and China

00:01:09.594 --> 00:01:12.321
that have been simmering for decades.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:20.528
So how did this innocent tropical fruit 
get caught in the middle of all this?

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:30.524
The complicated relationship between China
and Taiwan dates back to the 1940s.

00:01:30.524 --> 00:01:34.170
Back then, China was in the middle of a brutal
civil war between

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.674
the nationalists and the communists.

00:01:38.147 --> 00:01:43.130
When the communists won, they established
the People’s Republic of China on the mainland.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:47.297
The nationalists fled to Taiwan and 
called it the Republic of China.

00:01:47.297 --> 00:01:50.549
They both declared themselves the rightful
ruler of China.

00:01:50.549 --> 00:01:54.350
A claim that today only the mainland 
really upholds.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:58.520
Taiwan isn’t officially recognized as an
independent country.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.380
But it has developed into 
a self-governing democracy

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:05.099
with a constitution, legislature, and president.

00:02:05.099 --> 00:02:11.927
Since the civil war ended, Taiwan’s KMT
party has been in power most of the time.

00:02:11.927 --> 00:02:16.461
And while they maintained sovereignty 
they also grew closer to China.

00:02:16.461 --> 00:02:20.660
But in 2014, many felt they got too close.

00:02:21.187 --> 00:02:26.200
They passed a trade pact that opened up Taiwanese
industries to Chinese investment.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.207
And thousands of protesters stormed the government.

00:02:29.207 --> 00:02:32.382
[chanting] "Review the trade pact!
Review the trade pact!"

00:02:32.382 --> 00:02:34.884
They feared the pact would hurt 
Taiwan’s economy and

00:02:34.884 --> 00:02:38.030
leave it vulnerable to pressure from China.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.480
Soon after, Taiwan’s opposition party was
voted into power

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.157
for only the second time in the island’s history.

00:02:45.157 --> 00:02:48.888
And this new president continued to push back
against China.

00:02:48.888 --> 00:02:50.820
“We will not accept the Beijing authorities’ use of

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.461
‘one country, two systems’ to downgrade
Taiwan

00:02:53.461 --> 00:02:55.625
And undermine the cross-strait status quo."

00:02:55.625 --> 00:03:08.395
[in Mandarin] It’s been five years, and cross-strait 
relations are silent.

00:03:08.395 --> 00:03:11.299
Instead, China has intensified its pressure
campaign

00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:13.612
to unify Taiwan with the mainland.

00:03:13.612 --> 00:03:18.719
“Complete reunification of the motherland
can be

00:03:18.719 --> 00:03:24.143
and must be fulfilled.”

00:03:24.143 --> 00:03:26.762
Military incursions are on a steep rise.

00:03:26.762 --> 00:03:30.892
China has sent hundreds of fighter jets
into Taiwanese airspace.

00:03:30.892 --> 00:03:34.335
And they've conducted military drills designed to intimidate.

00:03:35.408 --> 00:03:38.840
They’ve also coerced other countries and
world organizations

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.330
from formally recognizing Taiwan.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:44.269
A big part of China’s pressure campaign
comes down to

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:48.085
isolating Taiwan from the rest of the world.

00:03:48.085 --> 00:03:52.316
But with this tropical fruit, China is doing
something different.

00:03:52.316 --> 00:03:55.511
It’s pressuring Taiwan from within.

00:03:58.021 --> 00:04:01.403
China is Taiwan’s largest trading partner.

00:04:01.403 --> 00:04:05.621
More than a quarter of all exports 
go to the mainland.

00:04:05.621 --> 00:04:07.933
And that’s in part because they offer incentives.

00:04:07.933 --> 00:04:11.407
Like dropping all tariffs on these Taiwanese
fruits.

00:04:11.407 --> 00:04:14.817
[in Mandarin] On the surface it looks like an 
“exchange”

00:04:14.817 --> 00:04:17.240
but in reality it’s a way to win 
Taiwanese hearts.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:20.551
[in Mandarin]It’s a comprehensive top-down 
strategy, wrapping around

00:04:20.551 --> 00:04:25.552
Taiwan’s agriculture, farmers and agricultural
products like a net.

00:04:25.552 --> 00:04:28.889
And this net can easily trap farmers.

00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:33.601
Like Hsieh who switched to growing atemoyas
exclusively 7 years ago.

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:39.059
[in Mandarin] The export volume was increasing 
dramatically.

00:04:39.059 --> 00:04:46.820
So we took advantage of the trend and switched
fully to atemoya.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.250
There was so much money to be made selling
to China,

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:52.929
that many farmers in the region also switched
to atemoya.

00:04:52.929 --> 00:04:55.301
And production tripled.

00:04:55.301 --> 00:04:58.692
This brought jobs and a more sustainable economy.

00:04:58.692 --> 00:05:00.624
But there was a catch.

00:05:01.352 --> 00:05:04.440
Because of all the incentives China offers
Taiwan,

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:08.381
a huge number of farmers rely on China to
make a living.

00:05:08.381 --> 00:05:11.391
And this creates a dangerous dependency.

00:05:11.391 --> 00:05:16.363
Because it allows China to disrupt trade flow
with, say, a fruit ban.

00:05:16.363 --> 00:05:18.457
That hurts fruit farmers in Taiwan

00:05:18.457 --> 00:05:22.740
Which could push them into blaming the government
for worsening relations with China.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:29.261
[in Mandarin] The motivations behind China's ban are 
politics and elections.

00:05:29.261 --> 00:05:33.270
[in Mandarin] China's ambition for Taiwan has always 
been unification.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:38.211
[in Mandarin] When they have patience, they might 
give you small benefits,

00:05:38.211 --> 00:05:41.962
hoping your impression of them will 
slowly turn positive.

00:05:41.962 --> 00:05:44.793
[in Mandarin] When they lose patience, they might 
create psychological threats.

00:05:44.793 --> 00:05:49.100
[in Mandarin] Like they are doing now.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.724
And while the threat might be aimed at Taiwan’s
government

00:05:51.724 --> 00:05:55.643
it’s farmers like Hsieh, who feel the impact
the most.

00:05:55.643 --> 00:05:59.684
Since the ban his income has dropped by more
than 50 percent.

00:05:59.684 --> 00:06:04.671
[in Mandarin] We need to help each other sell fruit 
without losing money.

00:06:04.671 --> 00:06:10.687
[in Mandarin] This is what we have to work hard on 
right now.

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:17.992
Atemoyas are the latest target, 
but not the only one.

00:06:17.992 --> 00:06:20.000
China also banned wax apples.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.318
And in early 2021, pineapples too.

00:06:23.318 --> 00:06:27.320
Just like the atemoyays, China claimed the
pineapples had pests.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:30.518
[in Mandarin] I was very worried and scared when I 
heard about the ban

00:06:30.518 --> 00:06:35.541
because I already invested so 
much money and effort.

00:06:35.541 --> 00:06:38.397
[in Mandarin] I was scared.

00:06:39.307 --> 00:06:43.270
Pineapples are the most popular fruit exported
to China.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:47.090
They account for about 60 million US dollars.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:52.310
So pineapple farmers are stuck in the same
cycle of dependency.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:55.970
But this time, Taiwan did something different.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:57.327
They launched a campaign.

00:06:57.327 --> 00:06:58.841
And it went viral.

00:06:59.011 --> 00:07:03.065
World leaders and diplomats posed with the
Taiwanese pineapple.

00:07:03.065 --> 00:07:08.289
And Japan and Hong Kong replaced China as
Taiwan’s top pineapple importers.

00:07:08.289 --> 00:07:14.176
Domestically, citizens bought an entire year’s
worth of pineapple exports in 4 days.

00:07:14.176 --> 00:07:18.449
Restaurants across the island added pineapple
to everything.

00:07:18.449 --> 00:07:20.965
And it helped.

00:07:20.965 --> 00:07:23.758
But dependency on China runs deep.

00:07:24.753 --> 00:07:27.218
China wasn’t just a big market.

00:07:27.218 --> 00:07:30.000
It was an especially profitable one too.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.943
[in Mandarin] To be honest, those sales channels are 
far from comparable.

00:07:35.943 --> 00:07:41.148
[in Mandarin] Elsewhere, costs go up by 20% — 30%.

00:07:41.148 --> 00:07:42.958
[in Mandarin] You can't make as much money if you 
don't export to China.

00:07:42.958 --> 00:07:46.610
[in Mandarin] It's a loss for us farmers.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.630
That’s because, If Taiwan doesn't sell fruit
to China

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:53.264
their only choice is to go north to Japan
and South Korea.

00:07:53.264 --> 00:07:57.584
Further south, in Southeast Asia, tropical
fruits are much cheaper.

00:07:57.584 --> 00:08:01.500
Longer distances are also complicated for
fresh fruits that require

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.449
cool temperatures and special storage conditions.

00:08:04.449 --> 00:08:08.067
At home, the Taiwanese government has offered
financial help

00:08:08.067 --> 00:08:12.488
but most of it is going to exporters and not
small farmers.

00:08:12.488 --> 00:08:22.188
[in Mandarin] The government wants to boost sales 
by subsidizing exporters.

00:08:22.188 --> 00:08:30.085
[in Mandarin] But us farmers have not benefited and we are
not happy.

00:08:35.211 --> 00:08:39.475
[in Mandarin] If you look at it from a strategic 
perspective,

00:08:39.475 --> 00:08:42.925
our enemy grabbed our Achilles' heel.

00:08:42.925 --> 00:08:47.904
[in Mandarin] This crisis has forced farmers, 
producers, and exporters

00:08:47.904 --> 00:08:53.577
to review this problem.

00:08:53.577 --> 00:08:58.648
[in Mandarin] They should've done this when 
dependency on the Chinese

00:08:58.648 --> 00:09:01.007
market was very high.

00:09:01.007 --> 00:09:02.446
[in Mandarin] But better now than never.

00:09:03.424 --> 00:09:07.341
So instead of trying to replace the 
deep-rooted market China created.

00:09:07.341 --> 00:09:10.682
Some farmers are starting to replace their crops.

00:09:10.682 --> 00:09:16.758
[in Mandarin] We have reduced production. I now
grow about 50% less than before.

00:09:16.758 --> 00:09:25.109
[in Mandarin] I also started to invest in bananas and 
taros.

00:09:27.084 --> 00:09:30.872
[in Mandarin] We don't rule out the possibility (of 
replacing our crops).

00:09:30.872 --> 00:09:43.120
[in Mandarin] We'll have to think about adjustments 
after this harvest.

00:09:44.451 --> 00:09:46.910
Because as long as Taiwan’s farmers are
trapped

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:49.589
in the middle of this geopolitical fight,

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:53.448
their livelihoods will always be at risk.

